    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full build compiled cleanly (including MapStruct annotation processing of the updated mapper expression) and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, with every derived value following from it.\n\n**New logic**\n- **`util/CustomerCode.java`** (new): pure-function util mirroring the other util classes. `of(region, telephone, lastName)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. `region(customerCode)` extracts the region prefix (used for locality).\n- **`util/LocalityResolver.java`**: added public `resolveFromPostcode(postcode)` deriving the region strictly from the postcode (\u2192 `UNKNOWN` when absent/unknown), per the spec's \"REGION is the region code derived from the postcode\".\n\n**Wiring the new identity through**\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`**: `generateCustomerCode` now takes the `Owner` and builds `region(postcode) + '-' + hash8(telephone, lastName)`, dropping the old per-city sequence numbers entirely.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: `locality` now derives from `CustomerCode.region(owner.getCustomerCode())` (the region-and-hash identity) instead of independently resolving city+postcode. `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` already build from `customerCode`, so they move automatically.\n- **Audit record** (`OwnerRestControllerV1`) already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so the create audit line now carries the new identity (confirmed in the log: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\nThe `customer_code` column (`VARCHAR(20)`) comfortably fits the new max-16-char format. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite are green.",
